  "dispatch": [
    {
      "address": "register",
      "sender": "$owner",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "event",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "$self",
      "program": "overlay"
    },
    {
      "address": "",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p"
    },
    {
      "address": "amm-p2p",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p"
    },
    {
      "address": "submit",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "filter": "beef"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/listTopicManagers",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "listTopicManagers"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/listLookupServiceProviders",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "listLookupServiceProviders"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/getDocumentationForTopicManager",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "topicDocumentation"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/getDocumentationForLookupServiceProvider",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "overlay",
      "fn": "lookupDocumentation"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/live",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p",
      "fn": "live"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/call",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p",
      "fn": "call"
    },
    {
      "transport": "http",
      "address": "/",
      "prefix": true,
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-p2p",
      "fn": "serve",
      "root": "www",
      "index": "index.html"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/swap",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "swap"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/addLiquidity",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "addLiquidity"
    },
    {
      "transport": "libp2p",
      "address": "/amm-validator/1/deploy",
      "sender": "*",
      "program": "amm-validator",
      "fn": "deploy"
    }
  ],
  "start": {
    "body": {
      "kind": "amm-p2p-start"
    }
  },
  "stop": {
    "body": {
      "kind": "amm-p2p-stop"
    }
  },
  "description": "An AMM over Mandala tokens (docs/AMM.md): the overlay engine (shruggr/skein-overlay 0.7.7, required: chain/1) with the Mandala components (shruggr/skein-mandala 0.5.2: the topic manager mandala-topic, one topic per token tm_<txid> and the discovery topic tm_mandala_deploys; the lookups ls_mandala and ls_mandala_deploys), the pool liquidity lookup ls_amm (amm-lookup, one service over every token topic, each query naming its token), the validator (amm-validator: swap, addLiquidity, deploy as libp2p direct calls; it submits the signed transaction to its own overlay by message, {fn: \"submit\"} in the box submit (<app>/submit), and answers the call on the engine's answer) and amm-p2p: the validator liveness beacon (a beacon event per served token topic, tm_<txid>-live, published by the host), the marketplace relay (amm.swap/1, amm.pool/1, amm.liquidity/1: a taker's or an LP's transaction carried to its validator) and the pages, www/ served from the app's own tree (skein-sdk files.serve). Anyone submits to the engine by message in the box submit (<app>/submit), and POST /submit admits there too (skein-overlay 0.7.6); the app's own box <app> is amm-p2p's. The manifest declares no topics: the owner registers each token topic with the engine, a message in the app's box register (<app>/register once installed) {fn: \"register\", args: {topic, program: \"mandala-topic\"}}, and drops it with {fn: \"deregister\", args: {topic}}. The owner starts the beacon with the manifest's start, {kind: \"amm-p2p-start\"} in the app's box, and sends it again after a register or deregister. A host serving a market (config.amm.ammP2p.market: true) also subscribes, at each start, the tm_<txid>-live beacons of the tokens it serves (subscribe {topic, program: \"amm-p2p\", fn: \"validateLive\"}, shruggr/skein#119) and keeps the validator map the relay picks from; a stop unsubscribes them."
}
